From 4f886624dd0c37c158b7099f0caa7260ead158e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1Pro-L4R8 <hoangquocvietbk2.13@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:06:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Refuse materialized views over tables under a row access
 or masking policy

A materialized view's refresh reads its base tables without the row access
and column masking policies of the user it runs as, and stores the result.
So a user under a mask and a row filter could create a materialized view
over the table and read every row and column of it in the clear through the
view.

Creating a materialized view is now refused (error 5212) when such a policy
on a base table applies to the creating user, and a refresh stops once the
user it runs as has come under one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
